CHAPTER II

PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

Article 2

The implementation and protection of women and children from victims of violence is carried out based on the principles of:
a. humanity;
b. respect for the rights of victims;
c. justice and gender equality;
d. protection;
e. non-discrimination; andf. best interests of the victim.

Article 3

The objectives of protecting women and children from victims of violence are to: a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and discrimination against women and children;
c. provide a sense of security for women and children who are victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
d. provide services to women and children who are victims of violence;
e. facilitate and mediate cases of domestic violence to realize harmonious and prosperous household integrity; andf. empowerment.

Article 5

Children who are victims of violence in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in article 4, also receive the following special rights: a. the right to survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic service needs;
c. the right to equal protection; andd. the right to obtain freedom;

REGENT OF SORONG,

Considering:
a. that violence against women and children is an act that violates the rights and dignity of women and children as human beings;
