6.4.text:
CHAPTER II

PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

Article 2

The implementation and protection of women and children from victims of violence is carried out based on the principles of:
a. humanity;
b. respect for the rights of victims;
c. justice and gender equality;
d. protection;
e. non-discrimination; andf. best interests of the victim.

Article 3

The objectives of protecting women and children from victims of violence are to: a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and discrimination against women and children;
c. provide a sense of security for women and children who are victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
d. provide services to women and children who are victims of violence;
e. facilitate and mediate cases of domestic violence to realize harmonious and prosperous household integrity; andf. empowerment.

Article 7

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 6 letter a, include: a. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
b. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence; and d. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with regional financial capacity. (2) The duties of the Regional Government in the protection of women and children from acts of violence in the form of: a. Implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence established by the government;
b. Collecting data and information about women and children in the context of efforts to protect them from acts of violence;
c. Conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence; and d. Conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.

CHAPTER IV

OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Article 6

Obligations and responsibilities in providing protection to women and children from acts of violence are the shared responsibility of: a. regional government;
b. community;
c. family;andd. parents.

Article 11

1. Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 10, is carried out by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of: a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual; and g. peace and order.
2. Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out in an integrated and sustainable manner.

CHAPTER III

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 4

Women and children who are victims of violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as human beings; b. the right to health and psychological services from the suffering experienced by victims;
c. the right to legal assistance;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidential handling;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process; andi. guarantee of rights related to status as family members and community.

CHAPTER VI

SERVICES FOR VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 12

1. Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence, are as follows: a. complaint services;
b. medical services; and c. medicolegal services for the purposes of evidence in the field of law. (2) Legal aid services: a. independence or empowerment services; and b. social rehabilitation services.
3. Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), are carried out by relevant SKPD in accordance with the programs, activities, and budgets available in each in the fields of: a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection;
d. mental and spiritual;
e. manpower; and f. education.

REGENT OF SORONG,

Considering:
a. that violence against women and children is an act that violates the rights and dignity of women and children as human beings;
b. that the implementation of prevention and protection of women and children as victims of violence in Sorong Regency has not been carried out optimally;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children from Acts of Violence;

