Article 3

The objectives of protecting women and children from victims of violence are to: a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and discrimination against women and children;
c. provide a sense of security for women and children who are victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
d. provide services to women and children who are victims of violence;
e. facilitate and mediate cases of domestic violence to realize harmonious and prosperous household integrity; andf. empowerment.

CHAPTER III

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 4

Women and children who are victims of violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as human beings; b. the right to health and psychological services from the suffering experienced by victims;
c. the right to legal assistance;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidential handling;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process; andi. guarantee of rights related to status as family members and community.

